  "description": "The 2026 election for Illinois's 2nd Congressional District is an open-seat race following the decision of incumbent Democrat Robin Kelly to run for the U.S. Senate. The district covers Chicago's far southeast side, southern suburbs, and portions of Will, Kankakee, Iroquois, and Vermilion counties. Cook County Commissioner Donna Miller won a crowded 11-candidate Democratic primary on March 17, 2026, defeating former U.S. Rep. Jesse Jackson Jr. and state Sen. Robert Peters. She will face Republican nominee Mike Noack, a truck driver who was unopposed in the GOP primary, and independent candidate Ashley Banks in the November 3 general election. The district is heavily Democratic and has not elected a Republican to Congress since the 1950s.",
